# Lines NoWayOS's tools/qemu-test must see, in this order: each core
# lists its threads in turn (the kernel's own lists, between these lines),
# then the heartbeat on core 0 keeps its time while the three spinners,
# above it on cores 1 to 3, spin for ever.
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: smp_heartbeat: the kernel's threads on this core:
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: spinner_1: the kernel's threads on this core:
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: spinner_2: the kernel's threads on this core:
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: spinner_3: the kernel's threads on this core:
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: smp_heartbeat: beating every 100 ms
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: smp_heartbeat: beat 3: on time
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: spinner_1: spinning from now on
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: spinner_2: spinning from now on
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: spinner_3: spinning from now on
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: smp_heartbeat: beat 4: on time
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: smp_heartbeat: beat 10: on time
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: smp_heartbeat: beat 20: on time
NOWAYOS: budget-probe: smp_heartbeat: 20 beats, every one on time

!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!late by
